---
title: "flash_loan - Flash Loan (Scallop Lend)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_version: check version == current_version
    q_check_version --> q_error_version: version mismatch
    q_error_version --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_version --> q_check_liquidity: version matches
    q_check_liquidity --> q_error_liquidity: pool_liquidity < borrow_amount
    q_error_liquidity --> [*]: abort error
    q_check_liquidity --> q_borrow: pool_liquidity >= borrow_amount
    q_borrow --> q_create_receipt: withdraw borrow_amount from pool
    q_create_receipt --> q_user_operations: create FlashLoanReceipt(borrow_amount, fee)
    q_user_operations --> q_repay: user performs arbitrary operations within same PTB
    q_repay --> q_check_repay: user returns borrowed_amount + fee
    q_check_repay --> q_error_repay: repaid < borrow_amount + fee
    q_error_repay --> [*]: abort error (insufficient repayment)
    q_check_repay --> q_deposit: repaid >= borrow_amount + fee
    q_deposit --> q_consume_receipt: deposit repaid amount back to pool
    q_consume_receipt --> q_fee_to_reserve: consume FlashLoanReceipt (HotPotato)
    q_fee_to_reserve --> [*]: fee (0.1% of borrow_amount) allocated to protocol reserve

    note right of q_create_receipt
        INV-001: FlashLoanReceipt is HotPotato - must be consumed in same PTB
        INV-002: flash_loan_fee = 0.1% of borrow_amount
        INV-003: no collateral required for flash loan
    end note

    note right of q_check_repay
        INV-004: repaid amount must be >= borrow_amount + flash_loan_fee
        INV-005: pool liquidity is restored after flash loan
        INV-006: flash loan is atomic - borrow and repay in same transaction
    end note
